---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/ui/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const updated = '13 August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy policy | ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`${SITE.name} privacy policy — how we collect, use, and protect your personal data, including compliance with India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act (DPDP) 2023.`}
>
  <div class="container"><Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy policy' }]} /></div>

  <article class="section legal">
    <div class="container legal-inner">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <section>
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p><strong>{SITE.legalName}</strong> ("we", "our", "us") provides Google Ads and Meta Ads management. You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="accent-underline">{SITE.email}</a> or <a href={`tel:${SITE.phoneRaw}`} class="accent-underline">{SITE.phone}</a>.</p>
        <p>This policy applies to our website at <a href={SITE.url} class="accent-underline">{SITE.url}</a> and to information collected through our lead forms, phone calls, and WhatsApp communications.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. What personal data we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact details:</strong> name, phone/WhatsApp number, email address.</li>
          <li><strong>Business information:</strong> business name, city, industry, website URL, current ad spend range.</li>
          <li><strong>Message content:</strong> whatever you share in the form's free-text field.</li>
          <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser type, pages visited, referral source — collected via analytics tools once configured.</li>
          <li><strong>Advertising data:</strong> Google Click ID (gclid) and UTM parameters, used to attribute which ad led to an enquiry.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
        <p><strong>To respond to your enquiry</strong> — contacting you about the audit or service you requested.</p>
        <p><strong>To measure advertising performance</strong> — gclid and conversion data help us understand which of our own campaigns generate leads.</p>
        <p><strong>To send marketing communications</strong> — only if you've explicitly opted in. You can unsubscribe at any time.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. How we share your data</h2>
        <p>We do not sell your personal data. We may share it with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Google LLC</strong> — via Google Analytics and Google Ads, for analytics and advertising attribution.</li>
          <li><strong>Our form/CRM provider</strong> — [PLACEHOLDER: name of your form backend or CRM].</li>
          <li><strong>Professional advisers</strong> — legal or accounting advisers where required.</li>
          <li><strong>Law enforcement</strong> — where legally required.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
        <p>We retain your data for as long as necessary to provide the service requested, and for a reasonable period after for record-keeping. You may request deletion at any time — see Section 8.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Strictly necessary:</strong> session cookies required for the site to function.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> anonymised usage data, once configured. You can opt out via browser settings.</li>
          <li><strong>Advertising:</strong> the gclid cookie tracks which ad click led to a form submission — first-party, stored on our domain.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Digital Personal Data Protection Act (DPDP) 2023</h2>
        <p>As a Data Fiduciary operating in India, we:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Collect only the data necessary for the stated purposes.</li>
          <li>Process data only on a lawful basis or with consent.</li>
          <li>Apply reasonable technical and organisational security measures.</li>
          <li>Notify you and the relevant authority in the event of a breach likely to cause harm.</li>
          <li>Honour your right to access, correct, and erase your data — see Section 8.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
        <p>You have the right to access, correct, or erase your data, withdraw consent, object to direct marketing, and request data portability where feasible.</p>
        <p>To exercise any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="accent-underline">{SITE.email}</a>. We respond within 30 days.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Security</h2>
        <p>Our site is served over HTTPS. We do not store payment card data. No internet transmission is 100% secure, but we take reasonable measures to protect your data.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. Third-party links</h2>
        <p>Our site may link to third-party services (e.g. WhatsApp). We're not responsible for their privacy practices — please review their own policies.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The "last updated" date above reflects the most recent revision.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>12. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>{SITE.legalName}</strong><br />
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="accent-underline">{SITE.email}</a><br />
          Phone: <a href={`tel:${SITE.phoneRaw}`} class="accent-underline">{SITE.phone}</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-inner { max-width: 42rem; }
  .legal h1 { margin-block: 0.6rem 0.4rem; }
  .legal-updated { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; font-size: var(--fs-sm); }
  .legal section { padding-block: 1.75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .legal section:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .legal h2 { font-size: var(--fs-h3); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .legal p, .legal li { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--fs-sm); max-width: none; }
  .legal p { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .legal ul { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; padding-left: 1.1rem; list-style: disc; }
</style>
